{#
    The Pi's complete Caddy config, templated by deploy_caddy.py as the
    single declarative source of truth (ADR-0008) -- nothing is ever
    hand-edited on the device. This is the templated evolution of
    services/pi-proxy/Caddyfile (built by
    .scratch/homelab-control-system/issues/05-auto-wake-proxy.md): the
    call_wake_api mechanism below is ported from that file. See that
    file's README (services/pi-proxy/README.md) for the full
    plugin rationale and live-verification writeup -- not repeated here
    to avoid two copies of the same argument drifting out of sync.

    Requires a Caddy binary built with the in-repo
    services/pi-proxy/wake_plugin module compiled in (see
    services/pi-proxy/README.md's Build section); that build step
    is not this ticket's concern.

    Per ADR-0011, this file carries no per-workload knowledge -- everything
    under /server is forwarded, path-stripped, to a single fixed upstream
    on the main server. Which path reaches which Docker service (Immich,
    AI agents, etc.) is decided entirely by a reverse proxy running on
    that server itself, not templated here.

    Deliberately does NOT proxy to the Server API: the browser calls it
    directly at its own tailscale-served origin (ADR-0001, "no Pi-side
    relay"). The Control UI is built (deploy_pi_api.py) with
    VITE_SERVER_API_URL pointing at that real origin, so the client --
    not this Caddy instance -- is what "routes to" the Server API.
#}
{
	order call_wake_api before respond

	# ADR-0004 hard requirement: never bound off-tailnet. An external
	# `tailscale serve` instance is expected to front this Caddy, exactly
	# as the Pi API/Server API's own bind_host convention
	# (services/shared/src/control_plane_shared/bind_safety.py).
	default_bind {$PI_PROXY_BIND_HOST:127.0.0.1}
}

# --- Single site: Control UI, Pi API, and the main server -----------------
# One origin, path-routed. `/wake` reaches the Pi API; everything else
# falls through to the Control UI's static files, except `/server`, which
# is forwarded (path stripped) to the main server as a single blind
# upstream (ADR-0011) -- this Caddy has no opinion on what's behind it.
:{{ control_ui_port }} {
	handle /wake* {
		reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:{{ pi_api_port }}
	}

	handle_path /server* {
		reverse_proxy {{ main_server_host }}:{{ server_proxy_port }} {
			lb_try_duration 3s
			lb_try_interval 500ms
		}
	}

	# handle_errors only works as a site-level directive, not nested
	# inside handle_path -- matched against orig_uri since handle_path
	# has already stripped /server from the working path by the time an
	# error propagates here.
	handle_errors {
		@server_asleep expression {http.error.status_code} == 502 && {http.request.orig_uri.path}.startsWith("/server")
		handle @server_asleep {
			call_wake_api http://127.0.0.1:{{ pi_api_port }}/wake

			reverse_proxy {{ main_server_host }}:{{ server_proxy_port }} {
				lb_try_duration 120s
				lb_try_interval 1s
			}
		}
	}

	handle {
		root * {{ control_ui_root }}
		file_server
	}
}
